  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...SFC high pressure will continue to build in \nfrom the west, while troughing continues aloft. This will keep \ntemps seasonable and mostly dry through late week. Showers and\nstorms offshore will continue to push eastward this morning. \nClimo temps expected through late week, with drier airmass \nkeeping it fairly pleasant for late July. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...The next frontal system will impact the area \nthis weekend into early next week, with increasing precip \nchances. Weak warm front expected to lift through the area Sat,\nwhile associated weakening sfc low approaches the Mid-Atlantic.\nBoundary will likely stall west of the area and/or dissipate \nthrough early next week, keeping the area unsettled with \nscattered showers and storms.",
